# =============================================================================
# S.A.K. Utility -- src/core/ clang-tidy override
# =============================================================================
# ACCEPTED EXCEPTION (R5-G12, tracked in docs/CODEX_REVIEW_5_REMEDIATION.md):
# readability-identifier-naming is disabled for the core raw-filesystem/parser
# layer. These are very large, lambda-heavy translation units (multi-thousand
# line APFS/HFS/PST/mbox engines). clang-tidy's rename FIX is unreliable at that
# scale: it produces partial local renames (declaration renamed, some uses left)
# that can compile only by accident and would silently change behavior if an
# un-renamed use resolved to another in-scope symbol. A false rename in the
# raw-block writers is worse than the style gap, so core naming stays as-is.
# The gui layer WAS renamed (smaller panels autofix reliably); core is the
# documented, permanent carve-out. Every OTHER check still runs on core.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming
